gave birth as a <i>zava</i>. … count … a woman who gave birth as a <i>zava</i>. … do not count","<b>a woman who gave birth as a <i>zava</i>.</b> These immersions serve to purify the woman from her status as a <i>zava</i>, not as a woman after childbirth. The Gemara answers: Beit Shammai <b>count</b> immersions that are due to the possibility that she is <b>a woman who gave birth as a <i>zava</i>.</b> In such a scenario, immersion is delayed due to the childbirth, and is performed when the woman’s impurity period of <i>ziva</i> following childbirth is over. Therefore, these immersions are considered as connected to the childbirth. But Beit Shammai <b>do not count</b>"],[6,8,"<i>ziva</i> alone."]],"w":{"0":"But there are","1":"a woman","2":"who … who","3":"gave birth … woman … gave birth","4":"as a zava … a … as a zava","5":"count … do not count","6":"ziva","7":"alone"},"g":[[0,1,"והרי יש","a"],[3,6,"הוא התנא לשיטת בית שמאי מונה","a"],[7,8,"כשלעצמה","a"],[8,10,"אין הוא מונה","a"]]},{"k":"916f2af3dc2f","n":15,"p":[[0,7,"the first week after she came before us, … let … immerse during the daytime","<b>the first week after she came before us,</b><b> let</b> the woman <b>immerse during the daytime</b>"],[7,8,"as perhaps"],[8,11,"each and every day"],[11,15,"her counting … are completed,","<b>her counting</b> of clean days <b>are completed,</b>"]],"w":{"0":"after","1":"the … week … she","2":"first","3":"came","4":"before us","5":"let … immerse during … daytime","6":"the","7":"as perhaps","10":"each and every day","12":"her","13":"counting … are completed"},"g":[[0,5,"באותו שבוע ראשון שבאה לפנינו","a"],[5,7,"שתטבול גם בימים","a"],[7,8,"שמא","a"],[9,11,"יום ויום","a"],[11,12,"מלאו","a"],[13,14,"ספירת שבעת ימי נקיים של הזבה, הטובלת ביום","m"],[14,15,"שלה","a"]]},{"k":"34ee8a498857","n":9,"p":[[1,2,"whose … is this … It is","<b>whose</b> opinion <b>is this</b> statement? <b>It is</b>"],[2,4,"Rabbi Akiva,"],[4,6,"who said"],[6,7,"we require"],[7,9,"counted in our presence,"]],"w